---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SubNav from "../../components/SubNav.astro";
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import Card from "../../components/Card.astro";
---

<Base title="Mechanics — Party Dungeon" current="/mechanics/">
  <SubNav current="/mechanics/" />

  <header>
    <div class="kicker">How it plays</div>
    <h1>Mechanics.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Four systems the game is built on, one page each. Cyan is settled, amber
      is still my guess.
    </p>
  </header>

  <Section title="The systems">
    <div class="grid">
      <Card href="/mechanics/party/" title="The party">
        <p>
          Classes with their own skills. Building the party is a core verb, not
          a character-select screen.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card href="/mechanics/maps/" title="Maps and portals">
        <p>
          Procedurally generated maps, entered only by portal, in real 3D space.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card href="/mechanics/dungeon/" title="The dungeon you own">
        <p>
          The base is a place you build in, stock, and open to the public.
        </p>
      </Card>
      <Card href="/mechanics/crafting/" title="Crafting">
        <p>
          Smithing, cooking, and alchemy, each held by a class. Items are
          designed by hand, not picked from a recipe.
        </p>
      </Card>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Underneath">
    <Card status="decided" title="Built in Bevy" tag="Yours">
      <p>
        Rust + Bevy. Greenfield &mdash; the working directory is empty, so every
        structure is a choice we still get to make.
      </p>
    </Card>
  </Section>
</Base>
